  "description": "We have configured the stream to pull video from **rtsp://192.168.1.10/stream** using TCP for the RTSP transport, and we are also ready to push the output to **rtmp://example.com/live/stream** if needed.  \n\nThe video path is set to encode with H.264 at a medium preset, a bitrate of 2000\u202fkbps, 30\u202ffps, high profile and the \u201cfilm\u201d tune. Audio will be encoded as AAC, also with a medium preset, a bitrate of 128\u202fkbps, stereo channels, and a 48\u202fkHz sampling rate. The primary delivery method is RTMP, while the HLS segmenter is configured for POST requests, a segment duration of 2\u202fseconds, a playlist size of 5 entries, and a timeout of 15\u202fseconds.  \n\nOn the player side we have enabled autoplay, left sound unmuted, turned on statistics, and applied the accent colour **#ff6600**. The player will display our logo from **https://example.com/logo.png** in the top\u2011left corner, linking back to **https://example.com**. Currently the repeat\u2011to\u2011local\u2011nginx service is enabled (and the user action \u201cstart\u201d is active), whereas the repeat\u2011to\u2011optional\u2011output service is disabled (user action \u201cstop\u201d)."
